{
  "id": "ss.relic.pendulum-chain",
  "name": "Barbed chain",
  "description": "The chain, not the head: four flat steel links and the three edge-on knuckles between them climbing from the lower right to the upper left with a slight sag, no cord under them, and eight bone thorns standing straight out of the links to either side, unequal in length and spacing, and the weapon's own head (`ss.proj.ball`) cropped to a dome at the bottom edge so nobody mistakes what the chain belongs to. The relic makes the chain itself cut, so the chain is the subject and the barbs are the change. The thorns stand perpendicular rather than leaning back along a shaft, and the chain is segmented rather than continuous — both of which keep it apart from ss.relic.whip's tapered feeler, which a second pass with a solid cord under the links had started to resemble. The links are solid with a darker slot painted on, not hollow: a first pass drew them as rings, and three rings with the panel showing through them were three eyes on a stalk. It stays off ss.relic.pendulum by showing almost none of the head that one is entirely made of.",
